// =====================================================================
// AP07 - Public Storage / SAS leak  (exfiltration in the Azure STORAGE PLANE)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
//   CHAIN (exploit):
//     1. ANONYMOUS enumeration of the public container 'public'
//        (GET .../public?restype=container&comp=list  ->  OperationName ListBlobs)   [T1619]
//     2. ANONYMOUS download of 'backup-config.json' (GET .../public/backup-config.json
//        ->  OperationName GetBlob) that leaks an OVER-PERMISSIONED credential:
//        a long-lived account SAS (leak_mode=sas) or the account key
//        (leak_mode=account_key) to the private container 'sensitive-data'.      [T1530 + T1552.001]
//     3. Authenticated PIVOT: the credential reads 'sensitive-data/customers.csv'
//        (AZRANGE{ap07_public_blob_to_sas_to_private_exfil}) and exfiltrates the jewel. [T1530]
//
//   Sources (REAL tables in Log Analytics / Sentinel):
//     - StorageBlobLogs  (blob DATA plane; resource-specific table produced
//                         by the diagnostic setting on '<account>/blobServices/default'
//                         with log_analytics_destination_type = "Dedicated". Without
//                         "Dedicated" the logs land in legacy AzureDiagnostics and the
//                         columns change name).
//     - AzureActivity    (MANAGEMENT plane; flows to the SIEM without provisioning anything -as
//                         in AP02-): captures the MISCONFIG and the listKeys.
//
//   MITRE:  T1530     (Data from Cloud Storage)                       [CORE]
//           T1619     (Cloud Storage Object Discovery)                (anonymous ListBlobs)
//           T1552.001 (Unsecured Credentials: Credentials In Files)   (SAS/key in the blob)
//
//   Sigma / KQL SPLIT (declared EXPLICITLY, like AP02 'the KV AuditEvent is not
//     activitylogs' and AP05 'the SAN does not travel in 4886/4887'): the DATA PLANE
//     (StorageBlobLogs: anonymous access + SAS/key pivot) is NOT a standard Sigma
//     logsource -> it is KQL-primary (THIS file). The MANAGEMENT PLANE (AzureActivity:
//     misconfig + listKeys) DOES have a companion Sigma rule (AP07-public-storage-leak.yml).
//
//   CAVEATS of the schema/telemetry (like the KB5014754 block of AP05):
//     * StorageBlobLogs is NOT active by default -> without the diagnostic setting on
//       blobServices/default, anonymous/SAS access does NOT exist in ANY SIEM. The
//       MANAGEMENT plane (AzureActivity) DOES flow without provisioning anything (like the AP02 misconfig).
//     * The PERMISSIONS and the SIGNATURE of the SAS are NOT logged: you see AuthenticationType=='SAS'
//       and from which CallerIpAddress / to which object, but NOT which SAS or its scope (it lives
//       in the signature, not in the log) -> correlation by IP/time/object, NEVER by the
//       content of the SAS (exact mirror of 'the SAN does not travel in 4886/4887' of AP05).
//     * 'SAS' (account) and 'AccountKey' are BOTH signed with the shared key -> they are exactly what
//       remediation kills with shared_access_key_enabled=false. 'OAuth' (Entra RBAC) and
//       'DelegationSAS' (user-delegation SAS) are the REMEDIATED forms -> they are NOT marked as a
//       pivot on purpose (they lower FP and teach the least-privilege antidote).
//     * The very lab DEPLOYMENT generates the misconfig in AzureActivity
//       (storageAccounts/write with allowBlobPublicAccess=true + listKeys to read the
//       connection string of the SAS): the defender SEES the vuln being planted (parallel to 4899/4900 of AP05).
//     * The lab container (azurerm_storage_container) is created via the DATA PLANE
//       (Blob REST API), NOT via ARM -> the lab apply does NOT emit the event
//       'blobServices/containers/write' in AzureActivity (SIGNAL C CONTAINERS branch). The
//       DEPLOYMENT telemetry is provided by storageAccounts/write (allowBlobPublicAccess=true)
//       + listKeys; the CONTAINERS/WRITE branch only fires if someone creates/changes the container
//       via portal/CLI/ARM/azapi (public-access flip by an admin or attacker), NOT in the lab.
//     * The account name carries a random suffix -> this KQL anchors on the FIXED container
//       names ('public' / 'sensitive-data') and on the leaked blob
//       ('backup-config.json'); set 'account_name' to the output ap07_storage_account if
//       you want to narrow to a single account. If your pipeline serializes the fields
//       differently, adjust against a real StorageBlobLogs row.
//
//   Managed COMPLEMENT: Microsoft Defender for Storage (native detection of
//     unusual anonymous access and exfiltration). Use in parallel.
//
//   Author: Azure Attack Range   Date: 2026-11-15
// =====================================================================

let lookback          = 1d;
let corr_window       = 30m;                   // window of the chain anonymous -> SAS/Key (OUTPUT 2)
let public_container  = "public";              // public container (container_access_type = "container")
let private_container = "sensitive-data";      // private container (the jewel)
let leaked_blob       = "backup-config.json";  // artifact leaked with the credential (SAS/key)
let jewel_blob        = "customers.csv";       // the exfiltrated jewel
let account_name      = "";                    // optional: set to the output ap07_storage_account to narrow; "" = any account
// 'SAS' (account) and 'AccountKey' = signed with the shared key = the surface that
// shared_access_key_enabled=false kills. We do NOT include 'OAuth' (Entra RBAC) or 'DelegationSAS'
// (user-delegation SAS): those are the REMEDIATED forms. Spelling variants are listed for
// pipeline robustness (OR, not AND; AP04 lesson of not silently discarding a branch).
let shared_key_auth   = dynamic(["SAS", "AccountKey", "Account Key"]);

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNAL A - T1619 / T1530 (data plane): ANONYMOUS access to blob storage.
//   AuthenticationType == "Anonymous" with a read/discovery operation:
//     ListBlobs             = the '?restype=container&comp=list' (enumeration, step 1)   [T1619]
//     GetBlob               = the download of backup-config.json (the credential, step 2) [T1530]
//     GetContainerProperties / GetBlobProperties = prior probing.
//   Anonymous access should NOT occur in normal operation -> every hit is suspicious
//   on its own (the GOLDEN SIGNAL). It is NOT gated by container or by success: an anonymous
//   FAILED attempt (403/404) against 'sensitive-data' is also valuable recon
//   (OR-not-AND; StatusCode is EXPOSED so the analyst separates success from probing).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
let SignalA_anon =
    StorageBlobLogs
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
    | where account_name == "" or AccountName =~ account_name
    | where AuthenticationType =~ "Anonymous"
    | where OperationName in~ ("ListBlobs", "GetBlob", "GetBlobProperties", "GetContainerProperties")
    | extend LeakedConfigHit = (Uri has leaked_blob or ObjectKey has leaked_blob)      // download of the credential
    | extend TargetContainer = tostring(split(tostring(ObjectKey), "/")[2])            // ObjectKey = /account/container/blob
    | extend Stage = case(
          OperationName == "ListBlobs",  "T1619 - ANONYMOUS enumeration (ListBlobs = restype=container&comp=list)",
          LeakedConfigHit,               "T1530 - ANONYMOUS download of backup-config.json (the leaked credential)",
          "T1530 - ANONYMOUS blob read/probe")
    | project TimeGenerated,
              Signal   = "A-anon-access",
              Stage,
              Plane    = "data",
              OperationName,
              AuthType = AuthenticationType,
              CallerIp = CallerIpAddress,
              Account  = AccountName,
              TargetContainer,
              Target   = Uri,
              StatusCode,
              LeakedConfigHit;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNAL B - T1530 (data plane): PIVOT with the leaked credential against the
//   PRIVATE container 'sensitive-data'. AuthenticationType signed with the shared key
//   ('SAS' account or 'AccountKey') reading 'sensitive-data' = use of the stolen
//   credential (step 3). The object is anchored by Uri OR ObjectKey (both are not required: OR-not-AND).
//   NOTE: 'OAuth' / 'DelegationSAS' reading 'sensitive-data' would be the REMEDIATED access
//   (Entra RBAC / user-delegation SAS) -> deliberately OUTSIDE this signal; that is why
//   RequesterObjectId (Entra identity) comes in EMPTY here and corroborates it is NOT RBAC.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
let SignalB_pivot =
    StorageBlobLogs
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
    | where account_name == "" or AccountName =~ account_name
    | where AuthenticationType in~ (shared_key_auth)
    | where Uri has private_container or ObjectKey has private_container
    | extend JewelHit = (Uri has jewel_blob or ObjectKey has jewel_blob)
    | extend Stage = iff(JewelHit,
          "T1530 - pivot with leaked credential: read of customers.csv (the jewel) in sensitive-data",
          "T1530 - pivot with leaked credential over the private container sensitive-data")
    | project TimeGenerated,
              Signal    = "B-sas-key-pivot",
              Stage,
              Plane     = "data",
              OperationName,
              AuthType  = AuthenticationType,
              CallerIp  = CallerIpAddress,
              Account   = AccountName,
              Requester = RequesterObjectId,     // empty for SAS/key (no Entra identity) -> NOT Entra RBAC
              Target    = Uri,
              StatusCode,
              JewelHit;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNAL C - MANAGEMENT plane (AzureActivity): the MISCONFIG and the key retrieval.
//   storageAccounts/write           -> possible allowBlobPublicAccess=true (ACCOUNT door)
//   blobServices/containers/write   -> possible publicAccess=blob|container (CONTAINER door;
//                                      'container' additionally enables the anonymous LIST = T1619)
//   storageAccounts/listKeys/action -> retrieval of the shared key (leak_mode=account_key / theft)
//   The VALUE of the misconfig (allowBlobPublicAccess=true, publicAccess=container) is NOT always
//   serialized in AzureActivity (the request body does not travel reliably) -> it is keyed on the
//   OPERATION and ENRICHED with a tolerant string search over Properties (hint, NOT a gate:
//   OR-not-AND). The very lab deployment fires here -> the defender SEES the vuln being planted.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
let SignalC_mgmt =
    AzureActivity
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
    | where OperationNameValue in~ (
          "MICROSOFT.STORAGE/STORAGEACCOUNTS/WRITE",                      // account misconfig (allowBlobPublicAccess)
          "MICROSOFT.STORAGE/STORAGEACCOUNTS/LISTKEYS/ACTION",            // retrieval of the shared key
          "MICROSOFT.STORAGE/STORAGEACCOUNTS/BLOBSERVICES/CONTAINERS/WRITE") // container misconfig (publicAccess)
    | where account_name == "" or _ResourceId has account_name
    | where ActivityStatusValue in~ ("Success", "Accept", "Start")       // real values of the modern AzureActivity schema
    | extend Stage = case(
          OperationNameValue has "LISTKEYS",   "T1552.001 - retrieval of the shared key (listKeys = full control of the data plane)",
          OperationNameValue has "CONTAINERS", "misconfig - container via ARM (possible publicAccess=blob|container)",
          "misconfig - storage account write (possible allowBlobPublicAccess=true)")
    // public-access hint (does NOT filter the row: the value may not travel in AzureActivity)
    | extend PublicAccessHint = tostring(Properties) has_any ("allowBlobPublicAccess", "publicAccess", "AllowBlobPublicAccess")
    | project TimeGenerated,
              Signal   = "C-mgmt-misconfig",
              Stage,
              Plane    = "mgmt",
              OperationName = OperationNameValue,
              Caller,                         // acting principal (objectId / UPN)
              CallerIp = CallerIpAddress,
              ResourceGroup,
              _ResourceId,
              ActivityStatusValue,
              PublicAccessHint;

// =====================================================================
// OUTPUT 1 - Unified timeline of the 3 AP07 signals (independent; union = OR).
// Triage of the full chain (exploit):
//   SIGNAL C (misconfig: the account/container are opened + listKeys)  ->  SIGNAL A (anonymous
//   ListBlobs = discovery  ->  anonymous GetBlob of backup-config.json = theft of the
//   credential)  ->  SIGNAL B (SAS/key reading sensitive-data = exfil of the jewel).
//   Each signal fires ON ITS OWN (isfuzzy supports the heterogeneous data/mgmt schemas;
//   never a global AND that discards a branch when a plane is missing -AP04 lesson-).
// =====================================================================
union isfuzzy=true SignalA_anon, SignalB_pivot, SignalC_mgmt
| sort by TimeGenerated asc


// =====================================================================
// OUTPUT 2 (high fidelity) - Correlate the public->private CHAIN by CallerIpAddress.
// The SAME client IP does, within corr_window:
//   (optional) anonymous ListBlobs  ->  anonymous GetBlob of backup-config.json  ->
//   read with SAS/key of 'sensitive-data'.
// The CORE is anon-get(credential) -> cred-get(jewel): near-zero FP, it is exactly the pivot
// that remediation (closing public access / shared_access_key_enabled=false) makes
// impossible. The prior list (ListBlobs) is joined with LEFTOUTER and ANNOTATED in PrecededByList:
// the chain is NOT discarded if the list is missing OR falls OUT of window -the attacker could have guessed
// the blob with container_access_type="blob" WITHOUT listing- (OR-not-AND, AP04 lesson; the fan-out
// of the leftouter is collapsed with summarize so the alert is not duplicated). CallerIpAddress carries
// "ip:port" -> it is normalized to the IP so ephemeral ports do not break the join.
// Uncomment to alert.
// =====================================================================
// let anon_list =
//     StorageBlobLogs
//     | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
//     | where account_name == "" or AccountName =~ account_name
//     | where AuthenticationType =~ "Anonymous" and OperationName in~ ("ListBlobs", "GetContainerProperties")
//     | extend ClientIp = tostring(split(CallerIpAddress, ":")[0])
//     | project ListTime = TimeGenerated, ClientIp, ListUri = Uri;
// let anon_get =
//     StorageBlobLogs
//     | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
//     | where account_name == "" or AccountName =~ account_name
//     | where AuthenticationType =~ "Anonymous" and OperationName in~ ("GetBlob", "GetBlobProperties")
//     | where Uri has leaked_blob or ObjectKey has leaked_blob
//     | extend ClientIp = tostring(split(CallerIpAddress, ":")[0])
//     | project GetTime = TimeGenerated, ClientIp, GetUri = Uri;
// let cred_get =
//     StorageBlobLogs
//     | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
//     | where account_name == "" or AccountName =~ account_name
//     | where AuthenticationType in~ (shared_key_auth)
//     | where Uri has private_container or ObjectKey has private_container
//     | extend ClientIp = tostring(split(CallerIpAddress, ":")[0])
//     | project PivotTime = TimeGenerated, ClientIp, PivotAuth = AuthenticationType, PivotUri = Uri;
// anon_get
// | join kind=inner cred_get on ClientIp
// | where PivotTime between (GetTime .. (GetTime + corr_window))
// // CORE (high fidelity): anon-get(backup-config.json) -> cred-get(sensitive-data) from the
// // SAME IP within corr_window. NEVER discarded: it is the pivot that remediation kills.
// | join kind=leftouter anon_list on ClientIp
// // The prior list (ListBlobs) is OPTIONAL -> it is ANNOTATED, NOT filtered. A ListBlobs from the SAME
// // IP OUT of window (or absent) must NOT drop the core. The leftouter may multiply the
// // row by each ListBlobs -> it is collapsed with summarize by the identity of the core.
// | extend ListedInWindow = isnotempty(ListUri) and ListTime between (GetTime - corr_window .. GetTime)
// | summarize ListTime = maxif(ListTime, ListedInWindow),
//             ListUri  = take_anyif(ListUri, ListedInWindow),
//             InWindowListCount = countif(ListedInWindow)
//         by ClientIp, GetTime, GetUri, PivotTime, PivotAuth, PivotUri
// | extend PrecededByList = InWindowListCount > 0
// | project ClientIp, PrecededByList, ListTime, ListUri, GetTime, GetUri, PivotTime, PivotAuth, PivotUri,
//           Alert = "AP07: anonymous-get(backup-config.json) -> SAS/Key-get(sensitive-data) from the SAME IP = public->private chain (PrecededByList=true if there was a prior anonymous ListBlobs in window)"
// | sort by GetTime asc


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// COMPLEMENT (management plane, high fidelity) - listKeys on the AP07 account by an
// UNEXPECTED principal = retrieval of the full-control key (leak_mode=account_key
// or key theft). Narrowing by Caller to an allowlist of known automation/IaC
// turns this into a low-FP rule (the lab's own Terraform does listKeys when
// deploying). Uncomment and fill the allowlist.
